06-10T21:09:13.992+00:00,nvme/Sensor 1,61.85\n124\t2026-06-10T21:09:13.992+00:00,nvme/Sensor 2,43.85\n125\t2026-06-10T21:09:13.992+00:00,amdgpu/edge,46.0\n126\t2026-06-10T21:09:13.992+00:00,amdgpu/junction,48.0\n127\t2026-06-10T21:09:13.992+00:00,amdgpu/mem,48.0\n128\t2026-06-10T21:09:13.992+00:00,k10temp/Tctl,48.875","structured":null,"error":null},"action_id":"evt_50d9eb7bf3b246439844b3c30ef49072"},{"id":"evt_57177646aff240e5b04fb33e3ab508b9","kind":"plan","source":"agent","timestamp":"2026-06-11T04:06:29.200135Z","schema_version":1,"seq":8,"meta":{},"summary":"Build a sensor dashboard with a Python backend (port 3000) serving CSV as JSON, and a Vite+React frontend (port 8000) showing a data table and summary card.","steps":[{"title":"Create Python backend API on port 3000","detail":"Write a single-file Flask app (server.py) that reads uploads/sensor_readings.csv, parses it, and serves it as JSON at GET /api/readings. Install Flask via pip."},{"title":"Scaffold Vite + React frontend","detail":"Create a Vite+React project in /workspace/frontend with npm. Configure vite.config.js to proxy /api requests to http://localhost:3000 so the dev server on port 8000 can fetch the backend."},{"title":"Build dashboard UI with table and summary card","detail":"Create an App component that fetches /api/readings on mount, renders a summary card (reading count, min temp, max temp), and displays all readings in a styled HTML table (timestamp, sensor, temperature)."},{"title":"Start both servers and verify in browser","detail":"Launch the Flask backend on port 3000, then start the Vite dev server on port 8000. Verify the page loads, the table populates, and the summary card shows correct min/max/count values."}],"revision":1,"context":"## What I found\n\n- **CSV**: `uploads/sensor_readings.csv` — 200 rows, 3 columns: `timestamp`, `sensor`, `temperature_c`. Sensors include nvme, amdgpu, k10temp, spd5118. Temperatures range roughly 32–63°C.\n- **Workspace**: Empty aside from the uploaded CSV — no existing project.\n\n## Approach\n\n- **Backend**: Flask (lightweight, single-file) reads the CSV on startup and serves JSON at `/api/readings`. No database needed.\n- **Frontend**: Vite + React, created with `npm create vite`. Vite's proxy config forwards `/api/*` to `localhost:3000`, so the React app on port 8000 can fetch data without CORS issues.\n- **UI**: A summary card at the top (count, min, max temperature) + a scrollable table below showing all readings.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- Flask over Node: simpler for a single CSV-serving endpoint, fewer dependencies.\n- CSV parsed at startup (not per-request): fine for 200 rows; avoids repeated I/O.\n- No build step for the backend — just `python server.py`."},{"id":"evt_0fd8062250ad4a5687db195da6958bff","kind":"status","source":"system","timestamp":"2026-06-11T04:06:29.232299Z","schema_version":1,"seq":9,"meta":{},"status":"AWAITING_PLAN_APPROVAL","detail":"evt_57177646aff240e5b04fb33e3ab508b9"},{"id":"evt_e8626deb2b1146a9ac9b22805f224596","kind":"status","source":"system","timestamp":"2026-06-11T04:06:29.580256Z","schema_version":1,"seq":10,"meta":{},"status":"RUNNING","detail":"plan_approved"},{"id":"evt_bc34ebb200714b359290e10c99cd4c53","kind":"status","source":"system","timestamp":"2026-06-11T04:06:29.583537Z","schema_version":1,"seq":11,"meta":{},"status":"RUNNING","detail":null},{"id":"evt_fa4dbede475e4b0ba04e588208fc2bc3","kind":"action","source":"agent","timestamp":"2026-06-11T04:06:46.397016Z","schema_version":1,"seq":12,"meta":{"risk_assessment":{"risk":"LOW","rationale":"plan-mode control signal 'plan_step' (no side effects)","analyzer":"rule_based","contributors":[],"self_assessed":"UNKNOWN"}},"thought":"Great — I can see the CSV has 200 rows with columns `timestamp`, `sensor`, and `temperature_c`. Let me start building.\n\n","tool_call":{"tool_name":"plan_step","arguments":{"index":1,"state":"active"},"call_id":"call_18878725f0464cb7bb9bdb52fd9ab604"},"self_assessed_risk":"UNKNOWN","llm_respo